body:
+1 to add as a new license, this one is also found on the old Xfree86 website at https://www.xfree86.org/4.0/LICENSE3.html (section 3.8).

This license appears to be tied specifically to Adobe's Display PostScript code, see for example [this Oracle notice text](http://pkg.oracle.com/solaris/release/info/0/pkg%3A%2F%2Fsolaris%2Fx11%2Flibrary%2Fdps%407.7%2C5.11-0.175.3.0.0.30.1483%3A20150821T173516Z) which includes the following lead-in: "_This package may include the Adobe Display Postscript (DPS) client libraries, which may be subject to one or more of the following notices:_"

@whot I'm not familiar with this space, but do you think `Adobe-Display-PostScript` as an ID and "Adobe Display PostScript License" as a name would be accurate(ish) here?
